#: index.docbook:324
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A template or mode name may is fully Qualified Name where the non-local part "
"is optional &eg; <emphasis>xsl:mytemplate</emphasis> is matched by "
"<emphasis>mytemplate</emphasis>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:332
#, no-c-format
msgid "Deleting a Breakpoint"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:334
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Firstly left mouse click the breakpoint you want to delete in the list of "
"current breakpoints. Then click the <guibutton>Delete</guibutton> button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:341
#, no-c-format
msgid "Deleting All Breakpoints"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:343
#, no-c-format
msgid "Click the <guibutton>Delete All</guibutton> button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:349
#, no-c-format
msgid "Enabling or Disabling a Breakpoint"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:351
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Firstly &LMB; click the breakpoint you want to delete in the list of current "
"breakpoints. Then click the <guibutton>Enable</guibutton> button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:359
#, no-c-format
msgid "Working With Variables"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:361
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If the inspector dialog is not showing use the <menuchoice> <guimenu>Debug</"
"guimenu> <guimenuitem>Inspect...</guimenuitem> </menuchoice> menu item."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:370
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Local and global variables are show in a tab on the inspector dialog. The "
"following example shows a XSLT code segment that declares a global and a "
"local variable"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: index.docbook:375
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&lt;xsl:variable name=\"globalvariable\" select=\"'foo'\"/&gt;\n"
"\n"
"    &lt;xsl:template match=\"/\"/&gt;\n"
"        &lt;xsl:param name=\"localvariable\" select=\"'bar'\"/&gt;\n"
"    &lt;/xsl:template match=\"/\"/&gt;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:377
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Clicking with the mouse on a variable in the list will cause summary "
"information to be displayed in the bottom of the dialog. If a variable has a "
"select expression, for example"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: index.docbook:383
#, no-c-format
msgid "&lt;xsl:variable name=\"changeable\" select=\"'oldValue'\" /&gt;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:385
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"then a new XPath can be chosen by entering a new value for "
"<guilabel>Variable Expression</guilabel> then clicking the <guibutton>Set "
"Expression</guibutton> button."
msgstr ""

